From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: give a clear error for a mesh vif under NSS offload when mesh is not built

NSS 802.11s mesh offload is not built for this 256 MB board (kuncy7 builds
it for his std group only; an active mesh costs RAM a 256 MB board cannot
spare). With NSS offload on, the firmware then has no mesh vdev, and a
mesh interface configured on an offloaded radio fails deep in
ath11k_nss_vdev_create() with a cryptic "-22 / unsupported interface type
7 for nss vdev alloc".

Refuse a mesh vif at the start of add_interface, when NSS offload is on
and NSS mesh is not compiled in, before any vdev or peer is created, and
log what to do. This does NOT keep the radio's AP up: netifd still wedges
the radio while a mesh interface it cannot bring up is configured (the AP
netdev stays carrier-down until the mesh interface is removed). What it
changes is the diagnostic - a line that names the cause and the remedy
(802.11s mesh needs host Wi-Fi mode, nss.general.wifi_offload=0) instead
of the bare -22. The guard compiles out if a future build enables
CPTCFG_ATH11K_NSS_MESH_SUPPORT. Issue #21.

Signed-off-by: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -7231,6 +7231,24 @@
 		goto err;
 	}
 
+	/* NSS 802.11s mesh offload is not built on this board (the 256 MB
+	 * boards leave it out; see ath.mk). With NSS offload on, the firmware
+	 * has no mesh vdev, so bringing a mesh interface up fails in the NSS
+	 * vdev create with a cryptic -22. Refuse it here, before anything is
+	 * created, with a message that names the remedy. This does not keep
+	 * the radio's AP up (netifd wedges the radio while the mesh interface
+	 * is configured), it just makes the cause clear: 802.11s mesh needs
+	 * host Wi-Fi mode (nss.general.wifi_offload=0). The guard compiles out
+	 * if a future build enables CPTCFG_ATH11K_NSS_MESH_SUPPORT.
+	 */
+#ifndef CPTCFG_ATH11K_NSS_MESH_SUPPORT
+	if (ab->nss.enabled && vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT) {
+		ath11k_warn(ab, "NSS offload: 802.11s mesh is not supported on this build; set nss.general.wifi_offload=0 for mesh\n");
+		ret = -EOPNOTSUPP;
+		goto err;
+	}
+#endif
+
 	/* an AP_VLAN ext vdev left over from before a restart */
 	if (vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP_VLAN)
 		ath11k_core_nss_stale_ext_vdev_release(ar, arvif);
